# Copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit real values — this repo is public.
# Everything here stays LOCAL: evaluations run from this machine via the CLI.
# No keys are ever needed in GitHub or GCP — the website reads finished results
# from a bucket and fetches nothing live.

# --- Local Bible-text cache (optional; speeds up repeated local runs) --------
# Where `bible-bench prefetch` stores Bible text and runs read it back from.
# Keep it gitignored; never commit verse text. Unset = in-memory only.
BENCH_CACHE_DIR=./bible-cache

# --- YouVersion Bible API access (required for ground-truth verse text) ------
# Provided out-of-band to authorized operators.
# YV_API_HEADERS is a JSON object of request headers, e.g. {"Header-Name": "value", ...}
YV_API_BASE_URL=
YV_API_HEADERS=

# --- Model under test --------------------------------------------------------
# You do NOT set the target key here. Pass it per run, either by exporting a
# named env var for that one command or by pasting it at the hidden prompt:
#
#   OPENAI_KEY=sk-… bible-bench run \
#     --base-url https://api.openai.com/v1 --api-key-env OPENAI_KEY \
#     --model gpt-5.2 --label "GPT-5.2" --gcs-bucket <bucket>
#
#   # or omit the key entirely and paste it when prompted (hidden input)
#   bible-bench run --base-url … --model … --label … --gcs-bucket …
#
# Provider base URLs (OpenAI-compatible):
#   OpenAI     https://api.openai.com/v1
#   Anthropic  https://api.anthropic.com/v1
#   Gemini     https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/
#   OpenRouter https://openrouter.ai/api/v1   (open-weight models)
#   xAI        https://api.x.ai/v1
#   DeepSeek   https://api.deepseek.com
#
# Reproducible open-weight scoring: pin the OpenRouter upstream with --provider
# (comma-separated slugs; fallbacks disabled). This fixes the provider AND its
# quantization. Ignored for native endpoints. Find slugs on the model's OR page.
#   bible-bench run --base-url https://openrouter.ai/api/v1 \
#     --model z-ai/glm-5.2 --label "GLM-5.2" --provider fireworks --run-version v0.1

# --- Referee for Basic Christian Theology ------------------------------------
# One pinned open-weight model plays attacker, judge and tutor. It must not be a
# vendor whose models are under test, or a lab would be both contestant and
# referee — which rules out Google (Gemma), and every Chinese lab on the board.
#
# Nemotron Super 120B, chosen on measurement rather than reputation: against 20
# real judged exchanges it agreed 17/20 and, crucially, cleared 10/10 of the
# cases where the model had NOT conceded. That column is the one that matters —
# Mistral Large scored higher overall but produced two false accusations, and a
# referee that invents concessions is worse than one that misses a few. Nemotron
# Ultra 550B is a touch sharper (18/20) and 9x the price; both err only toward
# leniency, so they inflate every model equally and relative ranking survives
# either. Set THEOLOGY_JUDGE_MODEL to override the judge alone.
HARNESS_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
HARNESS_API_KEY=
HARNESS_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b
